(the reaped status after a child exits with a known code. A child exits
 42; the parent reaps (blocking) and decodes the raw wait4 status word
 with lib/process.vox. The exit code must be 42, the signal 0, crashed
 false, and exited normally true. This exercises every lib/process.vox
 function against a real child, not just literals - which also proves
 the compiler delivers the status word correctly.)

see "../lib/process.vox".

Set pid to fork the process.
If pid is 0 then,
    Exit 42.
If pid is greater than 0 then,
    Set 'reaped pid' to reap child pid,
    Set status to the reaped status,
    Print "reaped pid matches: {'reaped pid' is pid}",
    Print "exit code: {'exit code of' of status}",
    Print "signal: {'signal of' of status}",
    Print "crashed: {crashed of status}",
    Print "exited normally: {'exited normally' of status}".